{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\n\nAn external architectural review graded rebar's engineering core near\n\"high-assurance internal platform\" quality (A-/B+ across architecture,\nconcurrency, CLI, MCP, CI) but its **public OSS/community packaging** a full tier\nlower (C+ community readiness, B docs, B library-API clarity). Every factual\nclaim in that review was verified against the tree: no `SECURITY.md` /\n`CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md` / issue+PR templates; `server.json` advertises only 3 env\nvars and the *deprecated* `REBAR_MCP_ALLOW_RECONCILE_LIVE`, omitting\n`REBAR_MCP_ALLOW_LLM` + `REBAR_MCP_ALLOW_JIRA_SYNC`; MCP tools carry no\nbehavior annotations; `pyproject` has no authors/keywords/classifiers/urls; no\nSAST / dependency-vuln scanning; no published API-stability policy or scale\nenvelope; the `run_workflow` docstring oversells a `daemon`-thread as\n\"resumable on crash\"; and the `rebar.*` facade returns bare dicts with no\ndocumented typed contract.\n\nThis epic closes the **OSS-surface gap only** — the packaging, community,\nmanifest-accuracy, docs, and library-contract layer — WITHOUT touching the\nfunctional/correctness roadmap already tracked in\n`docs/oss-comparison-and-remediation.md` (HLC ordering, authenticated identity,\ngit-gc growth). Scope was locked interactively with the maintainer; three heavy\nengineering items were deliberately excluded (see Scope · OUT).\n\n## Scope\n\n### IN (10 workstreams, decomposed into the child stories below)\n1. Community health files (SECURITY, CODE_OF_CONDUCT, issue/PR templates, SUPPORT).\n2. Fix `server.json` env/config contract + add a CI drift-guard.\n3. Annotate MCP tools with behavior hints.\n4. Enrich `pyproject` package metadata.\n5. Supply-chain CI hardening (CodeQL + pip-audit + alerts + attestation docs).\n6. API-stability matrix doc.\n7. Scale-envelope doc.\n8. External onboarding quickstart (single-sourced; defers to `rebar --help`).\n9. `run_workflow` durability-docstring honesty fix.\n10. Typed public library models (schema-derived TypedDicts, drift-gated).\n\n### OUT (explicitly deferred; not part of this epic)\n- **Durable workflow runner** (lease/reaper/resume worker) — separate effort;\n  only the docstring-honesty fix (WS9) is in scope here.\n- **Batched-commit bulk import** — touches the invariant-gated write path;\n  belongs with the functional-remediation plan.\n- **PR->Gerrit mirror bot** — ongoing service, contested vs. the Gerrit gate;\n  the redirect PR template (WS1) delivers the cheap substitute.\n- **OpenSSF Scorecard badge/workflow** — dropped: Code-Review/Branch-Protection\n  sub-scores read low BY DESIGN on a Gerrit-gated mirror.\n- **CI benchmark harness** and **SBOM** — deferred; docs-only scale envelope\n  (WS7) and CI-check-only supply chain (WS5) instead.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] All 10 in-scope workstreams are decomposed into child stories/tasks parented\n  to this epic, each with its own `## Acceptance Criteria`.\n- [ ] Each child ticket passes the plan-review gate (run in an LLM-enabled\n  environment) and, on completion, the completion-verifier gate.\n- [ ] No child ticket modifies the invariant-gated write path or introduces a\n  new runtime dependency into the deliberately-tiny core\n  (`pyyaml`/`jsonschema`/`referencing`); the typed-models work is static-only.\n- [ ] The OUT items above are NOT implemented under this epic.\n- [ ] `make lint` and the existing CI gates remain green after each child lands.\n- [ ] A newcomer landing on the GitHub mirror finds the standard community\n- [ ] The MCP `server.json` manifest matches the real config/env contract and is\n- [ ] MCP clients can render safe UI from tool behavior hints\n- [ ] `nava-rebar` presents complete, discoverable PyPI metadata (authors,\n- [ ] Supply-chain posture adds SAST (CodeQL) + dependency-vulnerability scanning\n- [ ] The public contract surface (CLI / JSON schemas / Python facade / MCP\n- [ ] An honest scale envelope (counts, throughput, latency, git-growth,\n- [ ] The `run_workflow` durability docstring states true crash semantics.\n- [ ] The `rebar.*` facade has a documented typed return contract (schema-derived"}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785007223191249001,"uuid":"4b8b5423-7aac-417e-9b67-00db5fcc972e"}